The jump edges of the scope rule vla_scope_exit covers the plain ones of, and
only the IR backend has any of it. The legacy backend gives a VLA's storage
back when the function returns and at no other point - the same design that
keeps it out of vla_in_loop and vla_scope_exit - and is not going to be taught
to, so this is skipped there rather than muted: there is no bug here waiting to
be fixed and flagged.
